papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-80-One-sided full shifts and their cylinder geometry are standard symbolic
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-81-systems \cite{LindMarcus1995}; random cocycles belong to the general
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-82-framework developed in, for example, Arnold's monograph
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-83-\cite{Arnold1998}.  The algebra also has a clear prior owner boundary.  If
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-84-one fixes a single prefix letter, the shift and prefix maps realize the
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex:85:bicyclic relation $DC=\Id$.  Normal forms, drift, entropy, and harmonic
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-86-measures for random walks on suitable groups and monoids have an established
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-87-theory, including Mairesse's treatment of zero-automatic monoids and the
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex:88:bicyclic example \cite{Mairesse2005}.  Ballot identities, first-passage
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-89-laws, and reflected random walks are classical probability
papers/93-random-push-pop-stack-cocycles/main.tex-90-\cite{Feller1968,Asmussen2003}.
